## 3. Key Decisions & Conventions
- **Card System Details** (data-driven population):
  - Cards are implemented as Godot Resources (.tres files in res://resources/cards/), each an instance of Card.gd (extends Resource) with exported properties: id, card_name, mana_cost, cascade_cost, cascade_gain, element ("neutral","fire","water","earth","wind"), art (Texture2D for full-bleed background), portrait (optional), type, damage, block, draw_cards, description.
  - CardUI.tscn (the visual prefab) has an @export var card_data: Card = null on its root node.
  - In the Godot editor: Assign a .tres file directly to the Card Data field on any CardUI instance for instant preview/population.
  - At runtime: Instantiate CardUI scenes (e.g., in hand or deck builder), then set card_ui.card_data = some_card_resource (from CardDatabase.get_card("id") or direct load).
  - Population logic lives in CardUI.gd's update_display() method (called in _ready()): pulls card_name → NameLabel, art → $Art TextureRect (full-bleed), description → RichTextLabel (with BBCode support).
  - **Costs**: Exclusive dual system — mana_cost (standard, resets to 3/turn) OR cascade_cost (alternative chain pool). UI swaps top-right CostLabel number + CostIcon texture (mana_gem.png vs cascade_orb.png) based on which is >0.
  - **Cascade building**: Mana cards (mana_cost >0) add cascade_gain (default 1) to meter on resolve if element matches current chain (tracked in BattleManager). Cascade cards (cascade_cost >0) spend from meter, typically gain=0.
  - element determines chain matching (per CardRulesBible): matching extends chain and adds gain; mismatch resets chain.
  - This strict data-visual separation enables easy card editing (change .tres in inspector), reuse of CardUI everywhere, dynamic loading from database, and clean saves (serialize deck as array of card IDs).
- Turns: Player goes first then resolve, enemy goes then resolve
- Mana: Resets to 3 at the start of each player's turn, unless modified by an item or card that round
- Naming: PascalCase for classes (CardDatabase), snake_case for variables/functions (draw_card)
- Signals: Use autoload Signals.gd for global events (card_played, turn_ended, battle_won)
- Adult Content: Mature themes via Dialogic; keep separate from core mechanics
- Save System: JSON files for decks/progress/inventory/story choices/faction standings; auto-save after battles
- Waifu Selection: Max 3 active companions; buffs only apply if conditions met (e.g. affection >5)
- Story Choices: Branching paths from player decisions; factions affected by help/hinder choices; culminates in demon invasion with multiple endings (world saved but losses, bad ending where demons win)
- Mobile Support: Planned for Android/iOS but low priority due to TOS concerns; touch input, responsive UI scaling, performance optimization
- UI Scaling & Positioning: No hardcoded positions or fixed pixel coordinates for UI elements. Use anchors, containers, and percent-based sizing/margins for fully responsive layout across resolutions (PC and mobile prep)
- Paths in Godot: All paths start with res:// (Godot's virtual root). Example: res://scripts/cards/Card.gd

